70 000  unused doses that could expire soon  because there's been this sort of  comparatively low uptake amongst the  under 30s  that would be a sensible move wouldn't  it  well we're working with universities and  there's a lot of comms going out at the  moment to encourage young people  to go and and get the job and actually  the ons survey did show that many  of our young people 90 i think said they  were likely or fairly likely to get the  job but of course  they haven't yet got round to it we're  working with universities to make sure  that that you know those comms  are those messages are are there and  people are encouraged to take the  vaccine  as soon as possible we will also i mean  in my local area we are setting up for  freshers week  uh we're opening up our vaccination  center which is very close to the  university  for longer hours so that we can deal  with that and encouraging  young people who haven't yet been double  vaccinated to start the vaccination  process so we will work with  universities we will do  what's sensible and of course you know  there are i mean  thousands of uh free appointments so  anybody listening if they're if they're  if they're up and listening and they  haven't had their job yet you can very  easily get  a walk-in now and get your first  vaccination and we would encourage  everybody  to do that okay i mean talking about  those young people who  don't go to university i know you're  unveiling a a new scheme to try to help  these  flexible apprenticeships but it's it's  seven million pounds worth of funding  well  in the great scheme of things how many  people can that actually help  well in the great scheme of things we  actually spend 2.5 billion pounds a year  on apprenticeships but what we're trying  to do now is to make  apprenticeships more widely available in  some  sectors where they found it difficult to  work with the apprenticeship system  specifically because you have to offer  somebody a job  for a year and sometimes they they work  on contracts or they work in project  bases  so particularly the creative industries  for example we've been working with them  to make sure that they can access  apprenticeships they're really keen to  get more apprentices and  and access a wide diverse pool of talent  all across the country  and this will enable uh many to do that  and also smaller and medium  companies to make it easier to have an  apprenticeship that works on a number of  different projects across a number of  different  companies but but still a high quality  training offer

